}
17. Can catch exist without try?

No.

18. Can finally exist without try?

No.

19. Can we write multiple catch blocks?

Yes.

20. Can we write multiple finally blocks?

No.

LEVEL 3 (throw vs throws)
21. What is throw?

Used to explicitly throw an exception object.

throw new ArithmeticException();
22. What is throws?

Declares that a method may throw one or more exceptions and shifts the responsibility of handling them to the caller.

23. Difference between throw and throws?
throw	throws
Used inside method	Used in method declaration
Throws one exception	Declares multiple exceptions
Creates exception object	Doesn't create object
24. Can we throw Checked Exception?

Yes.

25. Can we throw Unchecked Exception?

Yes.

LEVEL 4 (Method Overriding)
26. Exception Rules in Method Overriding
Child cannot throw broader checked exception.
Child can throw same checked exception.
Child can throw subclass of checked exception.
Child can throw any RuntimeException.
27. Can overridden method throw more exceptions?

No.

28. Can child remove exception?

Yes.

Checked exceptions are restricted during overriding; unchecked (RuntimeException) exceptions are not restricted by the throws rule.


LEVEL 5 (Custom Exception)
29. How do you create Custom Exception?
